{
 "translation": "I came to know what Kishwar was scared of. Trembling, she kept looking towards the adjacent room as if a lion would emerge from it and tear her apart. Shaukat! I wished I didn't let him go, I didn't know what to do. What terror had he instilled in the heart of this innocent girl that she would tremble at the mere mention of him? My resolve became even firmer. A steel-like hardness came over me. I will not only save Kishwar, but my hand, reaching far and wide, will bring thousands of helpless girls into the shelter. Like Rahat, all the girls of the nation will become servants, and then Hindustan will be free again and again. Free!",
